  ⚠ unicorn(no-useless-spread): Using a spread operator here creates a new array unnecessarily.
   ╭─[no_useless_spread.ts:1:37]
 1 │ function f(arr: number[]) { return [...arr.slice()]; }
   ·                                     ───
   ╰────
  help: `arr.slice` returns a new array. Spreading it into an array expression to create a new array is redundant.

