 1 │ function f(bufs: Uint8Array[]) { return [...bufs.slice()]; }
   ·                                          ───
   ╰────
  help: `bufs.slice` returns a new array. Spreading it into an array expression to create a new array is redundant.

  ⚠ unicorn(no-useless-spread): Using a spread operator here creates a new array unnecessarily.
